## Intellij
.idea/**/workspace.xml
.idea/**/tasks.xml
.idea/**/encodings.xml
.idea/**/compiler.xml
.idea/**/misc.xml
.idea/**/modules.xml
.idea/**/vcs.xml


## File-based project format:
*.iws
*.iml
.idea/

# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so

# Go binaries built IN PLACE. `go build` with no -o names its output after the package
# DIRECTORY and gives it no extension, so none of the four patterns above can ever match one --
# which is how a 69 MiB arm64 Mach-O binary came to be committed at
# go/rest-dynamic-controller/rest-dynamic-controller and went unnoticed (#564).
#
# Listed by exact path rather than by bare name: a loose `rest-dynamic-controller` pattern would
# also ignore the module DIRECTORY of that name, hiding the whole module from git.
/go/oasgen-provider/oasgen-provider
/go/oasgen-provider/oasgen-render
/go/oasgen-provider/main
/go/rest-dynamic-controller/rest-dynamic-controller
/go/rest-dynamic-controller/main
*.dylib
*.dat
*.DS_Store
**/bin/**

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Goreleaser builds
**/dist/**

# This is my wip ideas folder
experiments/**

# Dotenv files
.env
**/*.env

# Secrets files
**/password.txt
**/token.txt

# Crossplane stuffs
/.cache
/.work
/_output
cover.out
/vendor
/.vendor-new
.tool-versions
**/*.xpkg

coverage.txt
coverage.html

PROMPT.md
